    <!-- Tab info dialogs -->
    <string name="tab_info_overview">Top events and screens show what your users do most. The daily chart tracks volume trends over the selected time window. All data is aggregated — no individual user is exposed.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_projects">Manage your projects and API keys. Each project has a unique API key — create separate projects for different apps, environments (dev/staging/prod), or platforms.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_settings">Toggle demo data for testing in debug mode. The demo switch only appears when the server runs in debug configuration. Production deployments hide this by default.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_flow">Screen transitions show how users navigate your app. Each row represents one common path from one screen to the next. High drop-off at a step may indicate UX friction — investigate why users leave at that point.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_retention">Retention shows what share of each cohort came back at least N days after their first launch. Each row is a weekly cohort; the shaded range under a percentage is its confidence interval — with a small cohort, treat the range as the honest answer, not the single number.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_funnels">A funnel is an ordered list of events you already track, plus a time window. Each device evaluates its own progress and reports only how far it got — funnels are declared in your app's SDK config and appear here automatically once registered.</string>
    <string name="tab_info_experiments">An experiment shows two versions of a screen or part of a screen to different devices and compares how often people interact with each. Assignment happens entirely on-device — QuietMetrix never knows which device saw which variant, only aggregate counts.</string>

